  "definition": "The Basel Committee on Banking Supervision (BCBS) is an international standard-setting body hosted by the Bank for International Settlements (BIS) in Basel, Switzerland, that develops global regulatory standards for the prudential supervision of banks. Its accords \u2014 Basel I (1988), Basel II (2004), and Basel III (2010, finalised 2017) \u2014 set internationally agreed minimum capital adequacy, liquidity, and leverage requirements for commercial banks.",
